{#
  Template-maintainer note; a Jinja comment, so none of it reaches the rendered fragment.

  Cache ownership follows the dispatch handler's routing, not the dialect. A handler
  that routes through buildIngestorKernelCode hands it a KpackKernelLoader, and the
  shipped packs build that loader over a process-lifetime KpackModuleCache defined in
  their own native file. That pack owns the cache, so its row names a reset function and
  resetIngestorModuleCachesForTesting reaches it through resetModuleCache. The shipped
  hipkernel:Pointwise and hipkernel:ConvFwd packs both route this way and both carry a
  reset, Pointwise although its unit kernels are embedded_source.

  This template sees only the dialect. The packaged branch names a reset function,
  declared by ingestor_packs_hpp.j2 and defined as a stub by native.cpp.j2; the
  direct_load branch leaves resetModuleCache null and emits no cache. A direct-load
  implementation that caches modules owns that cache and supplies its own reset:
  define it outside the pack's anonymous namespace, declare it in IngestorPacks.hpp and
  replace the null field at the splice. README.md ("The five CMake/registration splice
  points") states the same rule for authors.

  The emitted rows are the fragment's contract: three fields, both branches, the null
  direct-load default and cpp_escape on the label. tests/test_fragment_contracts.py
  reads the first table row and the first reset reference in the rendered text, so the
  emitted comment lines may state the ownership rule but must never contain row text: no
  opening brace-quote, no ampersand-symbol-comma and no ampersand reset...ModuleCache
  reference.
#}
## Splice point 4b: .../kernel_ingestor_engine/IngestorPacks.cpp
## Add this row to the s_packs table. Both this edit AND the IngestorPacks.hpp declaration
## edit (ingestor_packs.hpp.txt) are required -- see that fragment.
##
## The struct is (label, registerSymbols, resetModuleCache). A row is valid with either
## reset value, so nothing downstream reports the wrong one:
##   * packaged/kpack kernels  -> &reset<Name>ModuleCache
##   * direct_load/embedded_source kernels -> nullptr, the default for a pack that caches
##     nothing; a pack whose implementation caches modules supplies its own reset (see
##     README.md "The five CMake/registration splice points")
## A packaged engine left at `nullptr` ships green and never drops its module cache.
## Check the IngestorPack struct before splicing: this row must match it field for field.
{% if config.is_packaged -%}
## Packaged dialect: this engine owns a kpack module cache, so it must drop it.
## Define reset{{ config.engine.pascal_name }}ModuleCache outside the pack's anonymous
## namespace and declare it in IngestorPacks.hpp beside the register function.
        {"{{ config.engine.name | cpp_escape }}", &{{ config.register_symbols_fn }}, &reset{{ config.engine.pascal_name }}ModuleCache},
{% else -%}
## direct_load/embedded_source: nullptr is the default for a pack that caches nothing. A
## pack whose implementation caches modules supplies its own reset (see README.md
## "The five CMake/registration splice points").
        {"{{ config.engine.name | cpp_escape }}", &{{ config.register_symbols_fn }}, nullptr},
{% endif -%}
